// [a Table of Contents.note]           a search in source files will find a reference to this file.
   ========================================================================================
   These PDFs try to answer the questions "what's in that note?" and "where is that note?",
   for notes somewhere in the ssDocs tree.  Each PDF contains links to files across the
   ssDocs tree in different directories; the integration of knowledge within SimpleSal
   is described by the collections of links to notes by topic.  Following a link in a
   PDF leads to a note; references in the source files to the note use the note's name.
   ========================================================================================

introduction
    ./ssTEA.pdf     Explain ssTEA as a separate and co-existing tree of features in source files
    ./SimpleSal.pdf Explain SimpleSal as an example of writing software that uses ssTEA features

time
    ./ssTime.pdf    Explain Real and Virtual Time concepts

events
    ./ssEvents.pdf  Explain Events: definition, instantiation, management

Agency
    ./ssAgency.pdf  Explain Events: sequences of Event Types granted Agency within Arduino's loop

ssTEA User Interface Application
    ./ssUI.pdf      A co-existing App, the UI has real time visibility into, and control of, Events.

simpleSim Virtual Data
    ./ssIO.pdf      How does a virtual pin emulate access methods the pin requires in reality?

mesa or platform
    ./mesa.pdf      What are the physical properties and limitations of the hardware platform?

   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// S~S  SimpleSal signal ends  S~S
